Author: Fukui Daichi <a.dog.will.talk@akane.waseda.jp>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-29
Description: Use the mpi module instead of mpif.h
 With mpif.h there are no interfaces for the MPI routines, so gfortran 10
 and later treat calls passing buffers of different types or ranks to the
 same routine (e.g. mpi_allreduce with integer and real arrays, or with a
 scalar and an array) as errors, and iteration_mod.f90 fails to build:
 .
   Error: Type mismatch between actual argument at (1) and actual
   argument at (2) (INTEGER(4)/REAL(4)).
   Error: Rank mismatch between actual argument at (1) and actual
   argument at (2) (rank-1 and scalar)
 .
 This used to be hidden by MPI compiler wrappers that added
 -fallow-argument-mismatch themselves; the mpif90 wrapper of MPICH 5 no
 longer does.
 .
 This patch replaces include 'mpif.h' with use mpi. The module gives
 each MPI routine an explicit interface, so gfortran checks every call
 against that interface instead of against the other calls. The interface
 declares buffer arguments to accept any type and rank, so the buffer
 mismatches are no longer errors, while the other arguments (count, datatype,
 communicator, ierr) are now type-checked. mpif.h is deprecated as of
 MPI 4.1.
